config BR2_PACKAGE_WIFI_ATBM6441
	bool "AltoBeam ATBM6441 (source)"
	select BR2_LINUX_KERNEL
	select BR2_PACKAGE_THINGINO_KOPT_MMC
	select BR2_PACKAGE_ATBM6461_TOOLS
	help
	  AltoBeam ATBM6441 (Hera) SDIO WiFi + Z7682 MCU combo driver,
	  built FROM SOURCE (github.com/gtxaspec/atbm6441) rather than
	  shipping a prebuilt .ko blob.

	  This is the first-class driver for cameras whose physical chip
	  is an ATBM6441 (e.g. Cinnado S2). It carries the Cinnado S2 /
	  T23ZN CMD53-survivability fix as a source patch
	  (package/all-patches/wifi-atbm6441/), builds z7682_disable_wdt
	  from recovered source, ships librtos.so for MCU watchdog comms
	  via /dev/atbm_ioctl, and selects atbm6461-tools for the MCU
	  WiFi/battery/PIR commands.

	  WiFi is controlled through /dev/atbm_ioctl (WSM), not
	  wpa_supplicant/nl80211 -- the firmware runs the MAC on-chip.

	  Distinct from wifi-atbm6461, which ships a recovery-extracted
	  blob shared by the B6/A1 cameras; select exactly one.
